{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"sase-zr.7.1.1:000001:issue_created:sase-zr.7.1.1:32c19668a9697880d4ed6993c215761f34efcd5f3f85b38f4729ae84a3ebab5f","timestamp":"2026-09-17T10:47:30Z","actor":"bbugyi200.apollo.sase-zr.7.1","operation":"issue_created","issue_id":"sase-zr.7.1.1","payload":{"kind":"issue_created","issue":{"id":"sase-zr.7.1.1","title":"Gate decision integrity: owned execution, durable failure outcomes, truthful completion","status":"open","issue_type":"plan","tier":"epic","parent_id":"sase-zr.7.1","owner":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","assignee":"","created_at":"2026-09-17T10:47:30Z","created_by":"bbugyi200.apollo.sase-zr.7.1","updated_at":"2026-09-17T10:47:30Z","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"description":"An accepted gate decision can never be superseded or cancelled while its execution owner is live; every post-acceptance failure (option command, terminal preparation or archive, side effects, follow-up, or owner death) leaves a redacted, durable, receipt-scoped failure outcome; attempt_completed is journaled only after the response is published; resume retries only the failed work; poll_gate and every waiting requester receive a failure result instead of a false pending or already_answered; and each failure publishes one deduped notification carrying resume, restart and cancel recovery.","design":"plan:202609/gate_decision_integrity_1.md","model":"","is_ready_to_work":false,"changespec_name":"","changespec_bug_id":"","dependencies":[]}}}
